From: nomorecoolnicknames <nomorecoolnicknames@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 16:00:52 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] SystemUI: notification shade reachable with a D-pad

Without a touchscreen the expanded shade could not be used: the initial
focus went to scrim_behind, a full-screen view, and no D-pad key could
move it (every item lies inside it). Two views take the focus that way:

- ScrimController made both scrims focusable outside AOD. A scrim is
  never a useful focus target; it is now never focusable.
- QSContainerImpl is clickable, which makes it focusable; focused itself
  it kept the D-pad out of the quick settings tiles. It now gives the
  focus to its children first (FOCUS_AFTER_DESCENDANTS).
---
 .../src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSContainerImpl.java       | 4 ++++
 .../android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ScrimController.java  | 7 +++++--
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSContainerImpl.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSContainerImpl.java
index d8bf990f6..09dc90b16 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSContainerImpl.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/qs/QSContainerImpl.java
@@ -70,6 +70,10 @@ public class QSContainerImpl extends FrameLayout {
         mSideMargins = getResources().getDimensionPixelSize(R.dimen.notification_side_paddings);
 
         setClickable(true);
+        // Being clickable makes the container focusable. Focused itself, it kept the D-pad out of
+        // the tiles, which all lie inside it (keypad phones without a touch panel): let the
+        // children take the focus first.
+        setDescendantFocusability(FOCUS_AFTER_DESCENDANTS);
         setImportantForAccessibility(IMPORTANT_FOR_ACCESSIBILITY_NO);
         setMargins();
     }
diff --git a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ScrimController.java b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ScrimController.java
index eb029aba3..fe4eec583 100644
--- a/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ScrimController.java
+++ b/packages/SystemUI/src/com/android/systemui/statusbar/phone/ScrimController.java
@@ -246,8 +246,11 @@ public class ScrimController implements ViewTreeObserver.OnPreDrawListener, OnCo
 
         // Scrim might acquire focus when user is navigating with a D-pad or a keyboard.
         // We need to disable focus otherwise AOD would end up with a gray overlay.
-        mScrimInFront.setFocusable(!state.isLowPowerState());
-        mScrimBehind.setFocusable(!state.isLowPowerState());
+        // Outside AOD a focusable scrim is no better: it covers the whole window, so in the
+        // expanded shade it took the initial focus and no D-pad key could move it on to the
+        // quick settings or the notifications (keypad phones without a touch panel).
+        mScrimInFront.setFocusable(false);
+        mScrimBehind.setFocusable(false);
 
         // Cancel blanking transitions that were pending before we requested a new state
         if (mPendingFrameCallback != null) {
